So again, a key point
here is we wanted

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:07.750
to make sure that when
your VM is created,

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.700
it comes out secure, right.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:14.810
So it's protected inside your
GCP project as a private IP,

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:16.420
and it's really up
to you to decide

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.220
how you're going to
make it accessible,

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.390
whether you want to open
it up to the internet

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.510
through a VPN solution or
a jumped server solution,

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:28.690
or maybe behind an
application server,

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.960
or maybe your intention is
to run a direct connect all

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.210
the way to your
on-prem data center,

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:37.350
and have connectivity all
the way from your data

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:41.410
center to the backing
power virtual machines.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:45.655
So we wanted to give you the
ability to fully control that,

00:17:45.655 --> 00:17:47.530
and we also wanted you
to be able to leverage

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:51.610
the rich diversity of
services that GCP has,

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:55.180
and their expertise around
networking capabilities.

